# Every search run against FindMyPast on 16-17 September 2026, with its result.
#
# WHY A LIST OF SEARCHES IS WORTH KEEPING. Most of these are zeros, and a zero
# costs the same as a find to obtain and nothing at all to repeat. The trial of
# 13-14 September recorded its negatives for the same reason and it saved a day.
#
# HOW THE TWO SEARCH BOXES BEHAVE — learned the hard way, and they are opposites:
#   lastname=   EXACT. «sojat» returns 0 and «sojath» returns 4, the same man.
#               A zero means «not under that spelling», never «not here».
#   keywords=   FUZZY, and it reads «Birth place as transcribed» in the
#               NATURALISATION set only. In the passenger lists it reads neither
#               the residence nor the ship — Eva Zubrinic's own record is not
#               returned by «prozor» or by «ultonia».
#
# AND THE COUNT ONLY RENDERS AFTER THE PAGE SETTLES. Reading it too early gives
# a false 0; four surnames were briefly recorded as having no records at all
# when Blazevic has 706. Poll for a DIGIT followed by «results».
#
# kind|query|set|result|what it means
