#
# 17 SEPTEMBER 2026 — the birthplace sweep, continued through the villages the
# 16th did not reach. Same method: `datasetname=united states naturalization
# petitions` plus `keywords=<village>`, which is the ONE record set on this site
# where the birth place is indexed. Every non-zero was confirmed by opening the
# transcript and reading «Birth place as transcribed»; nothing below is taken
# from the results list alone.
#
# AND THE URL FORM, because it was not written down and had to be found again:
#   https://www.findmypast.co.uk/search/results?sid=100&lastname=X
#   https://www.findmypast.co.uk/search/results?sid=100&datasetname=united%20states%20naturalization%20petitions&keywords=X
# The search host search.findmypast.co.uk serves the FORM; the results live on
# www. Guessing a record-set slug into a path gives 404, and `datasetname` with
# a display name gives 500 unless it is the set's exact printed name.
